  "text": "The largest eight-digit base 2 integer is $11111111_2$. To convert this to base 10, we calculate the sum of the powers of 2:\n\n$$\n1 \\cdot 2^7 + 1 \\cdot 2^6 + 1 \\cdot 2^5 + 1 \\cdot 2^4 + 1 \\cdot 2^3 + 1 \\cdot 2^2 + 1 \\cdot 2^1 + 1 \\cdot 2^0\n$$\n\n$$\n= 128 + 64 + 32 + 16 + 8 + 4 + 2 + 1 = 255\n$$\n\nAlternatively, using the formula for the sum of a geometric series, the largest eight-digit binary number is $2^8 - 1 = 256 - 1 = 255$.\n\nThus, the largest eight-digit base 2 integer in base 10 is $\\boxed{255}$.",
